# Linux-only server scripts

All server-side shell scripts under `deployments/` (and packaged `dist/install.sh`) are **Linux-only**.

## Rules

- **Run on Linux server only** — build, package, install, deploy, uninstall, start/stop/status.
- **Never run on Windows PC** (local Cursor shell, Git Bash, WSL-as-substitute for prod path, etc.).
- Agent must **not** execute these scripts on the Windows workspace; tell the user the exact Linux commands instead.
- Keep scripts **LF** (see `.gitattributes`). Editing on PC is fine; do not introduce CRLF — CRLF breaks shebang (`: No such file or directory`).

## Typical scripts (Linux)

```bash
# on Linux server, repo root or deployments/linux
./deployments/linux/build.sh
./deployments/linux/package.sh
# then
cd dist && sudo ./install.sh ./minigamesvr_*.tar.gz
```

## Wrong

```bash
# on Windows PC — do not
./deployments/linux/package.sh
./deployments/linux/install.sh ...
```
